{"authored" [{"question" "q-82624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2+4{x}^{2}-4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4385d0f6702ca6f8197ed3cc32c7f1c79cd2ae6f62bf5f1f7e599e97c1288a7" "basis" 1147 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-82624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2+4{x}^{2}-4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=4{x}^{2}-4x+1=(2x-1)^{2}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm (2x-1).\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int (2x-1)\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm ({x}^{2}-x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y={x}^{2}-x+4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4385d0f6702ca6f8197ed3cc32c7f1c79cd2ae6f62bf5f1f7e599e97c1288a7" "basis" 1147 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-82624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4e4b183965c62a7c75bfaa462ee8efd70fbadef48beebfed1b114ec3ed6029cf" "basis" 1147 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-82624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/state.json" "file_sha256" "f4385d0f6702ca6f8197ed3cc32c7f1c79cd2ae6f62bf5f1f7e599e97c1288a7" "basis" 1147 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14010575/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the arc length of $y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}$ for $x\\in [\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},1].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029846/state.json" "file_sha256" "d4c768da4efb408121081183c2faa4f28e3a3934e391b52a1eb499e0f24a2c5e" "basis" 1202 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029846/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}},$ $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and $b=1.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{(-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1-{x}^{2}+{x}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x){|}_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029846/state.json" "file_sha256" "d4c768da4efb408121081183c2faa4f28e3a3934e391b52a1eb499e0f24a2c5e" "basis" 1202 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029846/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029846/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9a7cb11605217c1c6bb1b419f93461fc14a60161bb4fe0cc680ff39d9347b1e3" "basis" 1202 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029846/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029846/state.json" "file_sha256" "d4c768da4efb408121081183c2faa4f28e3a3934e391b52a1eb499e0f24a2c5e" "basis" 1202 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029846/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-120752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{8}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029846/state.json" "file_sha256" "d4c768da4efb408121081183c2faa4f28e3a3934e391b52a1eb499e0f24a2c5e" "basis" 1202 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_A