sqrt{\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x){|}_{\\sqrt{2}/2}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-120752" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "16f1f4a5a74a783d73cf0a5469e5348e3c2b73357ea5d46657744a35fc26c68d"} {"question" "q-120752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-120752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-120752" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-122393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-122393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}={sin}^{2}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-122393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045