n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{1}{{(1+{x}^{2})}^{2}}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\pi .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-122394" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "16f1f4a5a74a783d73cf0a5469e5348e3c2b73357ea5d46657744a35fc26c68d"} {"question" "q-122394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-122394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2x}{1+{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\pi "] ["math" "y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{x}^{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-122394" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x-\\pi "] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-362547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the arc length $L$ of $y=\\frac{2}{3}(x+2)^{3/2}$ for $x\\in [1,6].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$L=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-362547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\frac{2}{3}(x+2)^{3/2},$ $a=1,$ and $b=6.$\n\nFirst, we find the derivative of $f(x):$\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}(x+2)^{1/2}=\\sqrt{x+2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}} & =\\sqrt{1+{[\\sqrt{x+2}]}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x+3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}=\\sqrt{x+3}$ to the formula for the arc length, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{1}^{6}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{6}\\sqrt{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{3}(x+3)^{3/2})|}_{1}^{6} \\\\  & =[\\frac{2}{3}(6+3)^{3/2}]-[\\frac{2}{3}(1+3)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =\\frac{54}{3}-\\frac{16}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-362547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "16f1f4a5a74a783d73cf0a5469e5348e3c2b73357ea5d46657744a35fc26c68d"} {"question" "q-362547" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"} {"question" "q-362547" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{38}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045363/state.json" "file_sha256" "3a31658266e9dc700108b14556371ebdfbfdcaad4e7749da8ea755ef1035eb32"}] "usage" {"q-82624" [] "q-120752" []} "basis" 1680 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186082473 17592186082474 17592186082475 17592186082476 17592186082477 17592186292706 17592186292707 17592186292708 17592186292709 17592186292710] "immutable_fields" [[17592186082472 :answer-field/correct] [17592186082472 :answer-field/id] [17592186082472 :answer-field/key] [17592186082472 :answer-field/type] [17592186292705 :answer-field/correct] [17592186292705 :answer-field/id] [17592186292705 :answer-field/key] [17592186292705 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
